From 0eeea5b4e4c6823f390396f29a040577f6af2f58 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fzdslr <fzdslr@qq.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 21:28:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] media: mediatek: decoder: force-extend av1 vsi on mt8188

The MT8188 SCP firmware uses the extended AV1 VSI layout but does
not advertise IS_VDEC_SUPPORT_EXT in its decoder capabilities.
Without this force, the kernel reads VSI_SIZE 0xD50 while the
firmware writes 0x1D68, the size mismatch check fires every frame,
mis-parses tile_group / reserved / cdf_table_size fields, and the
downstream MDP3 format converter eventually stalls on the
poisoned CAPTURE frame.

Mirror the workaround applied to H.264 in 6cd6c4fb (commit
"media: mediatek: vcodec: Use the extended H.264 VSI on MT8188"):
add a chip_name == MTK_VDEC_MT8188 OR-branch to the
IS_VDEC_SUPPORT_EXT guard so MT8188 always takes the extended path
without depending on the firmware capability bit.

Without this patch, AV1 decoding on MT8188 stalls the user-visible
"format converter stalled" loop in libva-v4l2-request after the
firmware's extended VSI is silently misparsed.

Signed-off-by: fzdslr <fzdslr@qq.com>
---
 .../vcodec/decoder/vdec/vdec_av1_req_lat_if.c        | 12 ++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/mediatek/vcodec/decoder/vdec/vdec_av1_req_lat_if.c b/drivers/media/platform/mediatek/vcodec/decoder/vdec/vdec_av1_req_lat_if.c
index e6b559797..993a7b801 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/mediatek/vcodec/decoder/vdec/vdec_av1_req_lat_if.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/mediatek/vcodec/decoder/vdec/vdec_av1_req_lat_if.c
@@ -1916,7 +1916,7 @@ static int vdec_av1_slice_init(struct mtk_vcodec_dec_ctx *ctx)
 {
 	struct vdec_av1_slice_instance *instance;
 	struct vdec_av1_slice_init_vsi *vsi;
-	int ret;
+	int ret, vsi_size = AV1_NON_EXT_VSI_SIZE;
 
 	instance = kzalloc_obj(*instance);
 	if (!instance)
@@ -1950,7 +1950,15 @@ static int vdec_av1_slice_init(struct mtk_vcodec_dec_ctx *ctx)
 		goto error_vsi;
 	}
 
-	if (IS_VDEC_SUPPORT_EXT(ctx->dev->dec_capability)) {
+	/*
+	 * The MT8188 SCP firmware writes an extended VSI but does not set
+	 * the IS_VDEC_SUPPORT_EXT capability bit (same bug pattern as the
+	 * H.264 driver, fixed by 6cd6c4fb). Force the extended layout on
+	 * MT8188 so the kernel struct matches what the firmware actually
+	 * writes. Other SoCs continue to gate on the capability bit.
+	 */
+	if (IS_VDEC_SUPPORT_EXT(ctx->dev->dec_capability) ||
+	    ctx->dev->chip_name == MTK_VDEC_MT8188) {
 		vsi_size = sizeof(struct vdec_av1_slice_vsi);
 		vsi->iq_table_size = AV1_IQ_TABLE_SIZE;
 		vsi->cdf_table_size = AV1_CDF_SIZE;
-- 
